### Introduction to RPKI Doctors
* **Slides**: [Introduction to RPKI Doctors](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-sidrops-sessb-introduction-to-rpki-doctors-00)
* **Presenter**: Job Snijders
* **Details**:
  * RPKI Doctors is a newly formed directorate chartered for a two-year experimental period to assist non-SIDROPS working groups (e.g., SAVNET, GROW) that are leveraging RPKI technology in their drafts.
  * The team provides solicited and unsolicited reviews to maintain architectural alignment with RPKI, prevent duplicate extensions, and avoid architectural anti-patterns (such as assuming IP and AS holders use the same CA).
  * A technical review checklist evaluates canonical eContent formatting, file naming schemes (to avoid race conditions), and relying party requirements.
  * **Discussion**:
    * Geoff Huston expressed skepticism regarding volunteer availability and high review standards, noting that traditional directorates conduct invited reviews. He cautioned against unsolicited reviews.
    * Job Snijders noted that unsolicited feedback sent to authors in other working groups has been positively received, as authors appreciate architectural guidance on ASN.1 and X.509 structures.

