### Post-Quantum Cryptography for the RPKI
* **Slides**: [Post-Quantum Cryptography for the RPKI](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-sidrops-sessb-post-quantum-cryptography-for-the-rpki-01)
* **Presenter**: Tomoki Yoshikawa
* **Details**:
  * Presented experimental results on PQC signatures and migration considerations for RPKI (draft-yoshikawa-sidrops-pqc-rpki).
  * Evaluated four configurations: RSA-2048, pure ML-DSA-65, Composite (ML-DSA-65 + P-256), and Mixed-tree.
  * Findings show composite signatures increase repository size and RRDP snapshot size by ~1.7x; RRDP deltas also increased ~1.7x (dominated by CRLs and manifests). Validation was tested using modified Rpki-client and Routinator backends.
  * Requested working group adoption as an informational document to capture experimental evidence.
  * **Discussion**:
    * Russ Housley noted that in addition to object sizes, the document must integrate key rollover mechanisms defined in RFC 6916 to address full ecosystem transitions.
    * Job Snijders supported adoption as an informational log of experimental observations to help quantify system growth.
    * Tim Bruijnzeels highlighted that RRDP delta churn is heavily influenced by CA reissuance intervals (ranging from 16 hours to 2 days) and suggested that protocols like draft-ietf-sidrops-rpki-erik-protocol could enable slower reissuance strategies to mitigate size increases.

