### BGP Signed Origin Delegation Attestation (SODA)
* **Slides**: [BGP Signed Origin Delegation Attestation (SODA)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-sidrops-sessb-bgp-signed-origin-delegation-attestation-soda-00)
* **Presenter**: Forest
* **Details**:
  * Proposed a new BGP optional transitive path attribute (SODA) to distinguish legitimate Multiple Origin AS (MOAS) operations (e.g., CDNs, DDoS mitigation) from route hijacking when ROV evaluates to "invalid".
  * SODA carries a delegator-signed statement (prefix, delegated AS, expiration time) directly inside BGP UPDATE messages.
  * If ROV returns invalid, a SODA-aware router validates the signature and delegation parameters to accept the route under local policy.
  * **Discussion**:
    * A participant queried whether SODA is attempting to work around slow RPKI propagation/dynamics, suggesting it would be preferable to address RPKI dynamic updates directly rather than adding BGP attributes.

