### Information Asymmetry and Deployment Gaps in RPKI-based Route Origin Validation
* **Slides**: [Information Asymmetry and Deployment Gaps in RPKI-based Route Origin Validation](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/information-asymmetry-and-deployment-gaps-in-rpki-based-route-origin-validation-01)
* **Presenter**: Presenter on behalf of authors
* **Details**:
  * Analyzed why small/long-tail ISPs hesitate to enforce strict ROV invalid dropping due to control plane asymmetry, configuration delays, and high operational risk of false positives.
  * Proposed origin-side cross-validation where the origin AS checks announcements against its local RPKI cache prior to advertising.
  * *Note*: Presentation was truncated as the session reached its time limit.

